data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":87,"item_id":"rs_03db426b89ea6e84016aca98ae47988194801c0420760218e5","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering file operations**\n\nI'm pondering whether to append a test to an existing file while using a unique tail. There's a question about whether I should create a new file with my own helper instead. It seems acceptable to duplicate the existing helper, which isn't exported. But maybe it would be simpler to just create a new file to test with the helper, keeping it compact. I want to make sure I choose the best approach for this task!"}

